WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.000
Welcome to CampusMate MCP, built by team Logic Squad for Track 1: Make MCP Matter.

00:00:06.500 --> 00:00:13.000
CampusMate solves an everyday student challenge: managing academic life through an AI assistant you can truly trust.

00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:20.000
Our guiding rule: Your college life, in your AI assistant, and nothing happens without your yes.

00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:27.500
Everyday student life is scattered across attendance portals, WhatsApp circulars, Google Classroom, and timetable photos.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:34.500
Missing the 75% attendance cutoff can mean exam debarment. Writing to faculty takes endless hesitation.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:45.000
Generic chatbots are blind to personal student data, and students cannot trust autonomous bots to send emails or change records.

00:00:45.500 --> 00:00:53.000
Enter CampusMate MCP: an open Model Context Protocol server paired with a dedicated companion student dashboard.

00:00:53.500 --> 00:01:01.000
The AI assistant gains rich, structured context about classes, assignments, circulars, and attendance.

00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:10.000
Our core governance guarantee: The AI can only propose. Only the student can approve in the dashboard.

00:01:10.500 --> 00:01:18.500
Let's see a live demonstration. A student asks Claude: "Can I skip Operating Systems class tomorrow?"

00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:26.500
CampusMate executes get_attendance. Using deterministic code math, it computes 40 of 52 classes attended: 76.9%.

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:34.000
The AI reports: "You can miss 1 more class and remain above 75%." Zero mathematical hallucination.

00:01:34.500 --> 00:01:42.500
Next, the student asks: "Email Professor Rao for a 2-day extension on the DBMS assignment."

00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:50.000
The AI calls draft_faculty_email. It does not send an email—it creates a pending card in CampusMate.

00:01:50.500 --> 00:01:55.000
In the dashboard, the student reviews the verified recipient, edits the draft, and clicks Approve.

00:01:55.500 --> 00:02:02.500
Why does MCP matter? It transforms conversational AI into a grounded everyday assistant connected to real databases.

00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:10.500
Our dual-channel architecture strictly isolates the AI's Bearer token from the dashboard's authenticated session cookie.

00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:18.000
The MCP endpoint has zero approval tools. The AI literally cannot approve its own proposals.

00:02:18.500 --> 00:02:25.000
Per-tool permission killswitches let students disable any capability instantly with full transparency in the Activity log.

00:02:25.500 --> 00:02:32.000
Even when untrusted circulars contain prompt injection, the attack is safely contained to a pending card that is easily rejected.

00:02:32.500 --> 00:02:39.000
CampusMate is built on Node 24 with native TypeScript, Hono, SQLite, React 19, and the official MCP SDK.

00:02:39.500 --> 00:02:45.000
It is verified by 239 automated tests with 96% code coverage and deployed live on Render.

00:02:45.500 --> 00:02:53.000
CampusMate makes MCP matter by providing everyday student utility protected by unwavering human consent.

00:02:53.500 --> 00:03:00.000
We are Team Logic Squad for Track 1: Make MCP Matter. Thank you!
